# How to install

>>> If you already have virtualenvwrapper installed <<<

1. Navigate to this folder within the terminal -> cd ~/user.../path/peer_graded_assign_wk2

2. Create virtual environment with the command -> mkvirtualenv <name>

3. Activate venv -> workon <name>

4. Install the dependencies using -> pip install -r requirements.txt

>>> If you don't have virtualenvwrapper installed <<<

1. Install virtualenvwrapper -> pip3 install virtualenvwrapper

... then follow steps 2 to 4 from the section above.
